      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a Provider**\n\nI'm currently leaning towards AWS SQS for this dead-letter queue implementation. It seems like a solid choice for a message queuing service with excellent dead-letter queue support. I'm aiming to create a Python file, `dead_letter.py`, to handle this functionality.\n\n\n**Implementing the Functionality**\n\nI'm now focused on the concrete implementation, deciding to use AWS SQS and the `boto3` library. My next step involves constructing the `dead_letter.py` file, incorporating a function to route failed messages to the dead-letter queue. I plan to use provider-specific identifiers like `boto3`, `sqs`, and `QueueUrl` to ensure proper integration.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863574303,
          "start": 1789863571961
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc2eb1f9001EaLOs86mQT39rS",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc2eadf4001v6eCvjfvCml5FJ",
      "session_id": "ses_f43d1521affea0Gaf3OD62fM06",
