        "text": "**Constructing Dead-Letter Script**\n\nI've just finished the initial setup for the `dead_letter.py` script. I've utilized `boto3` to interact with AWS SQS and handle message transfers. The code is structured to accommodate the necessary provider-specific details like `boto3.client('sqs')` and `QueueUrl`. I've also incorporated example usage with environment variables to illustrate its implementation.\n\n\n**Defining Message Handler**\n\nThe `dead_letter.py` script now handles message transfer using `boto3` and AWS SQS. The architecture accounts for provider-specific credentials. It includes example configurations with environment variables, showcasing how to use the script. This gives a functional starting point that I can now refine with more specifics.\n\n\n",
